  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Progressive cycle",
      "items": [
        "① Resolve: requiredWhen decides applicability (unknown → blocked); dependsOn and readyWhen decide readiness; a result counts only if its input fingerprint matches",
        "② Plan: collect:<field> for each missing human field (rendered as the form); <activity>:<fingerprint> once per input set",
        "③ Execute: people answer through Updates while independent activities run concurrently",
        "④ Every answer, result and retry enters the inbox; one loop applies it, bumps the revision and repeats until every applicable requirement is satisfied"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Branching follow-up forms",
      "items": [
        "On completion, the first next entry whose when holds (outcome and data) is chosen",
        "Continue-as-new keeps the workflow ID and starts a fresh history; final values become read-only context (application.*, offer.*)",
        "loan_application → loan_offer → disbursement or offer_feedback; unaffordable only → affordability_review"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Stale-safe results",
      "items": [
        "Action id = activity:input-fingerprint, so re-planning never duplicates work",
        "Results are keyed by fingerprint; only the current inputs' result satisfies a requirement",
        "Corrections retire non-applicable values to an audit list"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Submissions and durability",
      "items": [
        "Update validator rejects bad shapes; the loop re-checks per-field conflicts (422 / 409)",
        "Submission id is the Update ID, plus in-state dedupe",
        "Schema pinned in history; worker restarts replay without rerunning completed checks",
        "Activities are scheduled through Temporal; drawn direct for clarity"
      ]
    }
  ]
